{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/proposedviewsize"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ProposedViewSize"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"During layout in SwiftUI, views choose their own size, but they do that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in response to a size proposal from their parent view. When you create","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a custom layout using the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout","type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol, your layout container","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"participates in this process using ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProposedViewSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The layout protocol’s methods take a proposed size input that you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can take into account when arranging views and calculating the size of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the composite container. Similarly, your layout proposes a size to each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its own subviews when it measures and places them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Layout containers typically measure their subviews by proposing several"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sizes and looking at the responses. The container can use this information"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to decide how to allocate space among its subviews. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout might try the following special proposals:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/zero","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" proposal; the view responds with its minimum size."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/infinity","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" proposal; the view responds with its maximum size."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/unspecified","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" proposal; the view responds with its ideal size.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A layout might also try special cases for one dimension at a time. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HStack"},{"text":" might measure the flexibility of its subviews’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"widths, while using a fixed value for the height.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI16ProposedViewSizeV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ProposedViewSize"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ProposedViewSize","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","